english:
General Legal Framework for Electronic Commerce and Electronic Signatures, Art. 53(2)

CHAPTER V, Section II, Art. 53, p.36 :: guros

1. The electronic commerce merchant uses secure technologies and protocols to safeguard the transmission and reception of online payments and other private or sensitive information.

2. For any product or service ordered from the electronic commerce merchant, the following information shall be provided to the buyer prior to the completion of the purchase:

a) The total price of the product or service, including any currency conversion fee, tax or delivery fee for the selected delivery method, in itemized form and listed separately;

b) The payment methods accepted by the electronic commerce merchant;

c) The alternatives for return, repair or replacement of a purchased product, as well as the deadlines applicable to each of them, in the event that the product delivered to the buyer is defective or does not correspond to the product description presented on the electronic marketing and sales website of the electronic commerce merchant;

d) The period of time and the method through which a product delivered to the buyer may be returned to the seller, such period being no less than seven business days, and the division of costs, if applicable, between the seller and the buyer for any returned product, unless the reason for the return is that the product is defective or is not in conformity with the product description provided by the electronic commerce merchant prior to its sale to the buyer, in which case the seller must bear the entire cost of the product's return.

